{
 "id": "present-simple",
 "title": "Le présent simple",
 "level": "A1",
 "topic": "Temps verbaux",
 "summary": "Habitudes, vérités générales et horaires : règle du -s, do/does et adverbes de fréquence.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "À quoi sert-il ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Une **habitude** : *I check my mails every morning.*",
    "Une **vérité générale** : *Water boils at 100 °C.*",
    "Un **horaire** : *The train leaves at 8.*",
    "Un état (*know, like, need, want*) : *I need help.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Affirmative : la règle du -s"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "À toutes les personnes, c'est le **verbe de base**, sauf à **he / she / it** où l'on ajoute **-s** : *she works*."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Fin du verbe",
    "Règle",
    "Exemple"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "la plupart",
     "+ s",
     "work → works"
    ],
    [
     "-s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o",
     "+ es",
     "watch → watches, go → goes"
    ],
    [
     "consonne + y",
     "y → ies",
     "study → studies"
    ],
    [
     "voyelle + y",
     "+ s",
     "play → plays"
    ],
    [
     "have",
     "irrégulier",
     "have → has"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Négation et question"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "On utilise l'auxiliaire **do** (ou **does** à la 3e personne). Le verbe reste alors **à l'infinitif sans -s** : le -s est déjà porté par *does*."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "",
    "Négation",
    "Question"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I / you / we / they",
     "I don't work",
     "Do you work?"
    ],
    [
     "he / she / it",
     "She doesn't work",
     "Does she work?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Adverbes de fréquence"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "*always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely, never* se placent **avant le verbe principal** mais **après to be** : *I **always** check logs.* / *He **is never** late.*"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Exemples"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "She works as a developer.",
   "fr": "Elle travaille comme développeuse."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "Does your team use Linux?",
   "fr": "Ton équipe utilise-t-elle Linux ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "He doesn't like meetings.",
   "fr": "Il n'aime pas les réunions."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "I usually take the train.",
   "fr": "Je prends généralement le train."
  },
  {
   "type": "tip",
   "text": "**Piège** : *Does she **works**?* est faux. Après does, le verbe est nu : *Does she work?*"
  }
 ],
